# action.seq — canonical per-category action order for the TIDL toolchain.
#
# TIDL method ids are positional within a category interface. Both the
# toolchain (actionc, at code generation) and the device runtime read this
# file to agree on that order. Rules:
#   * One [Category] section per TIDL category; one action name per line.
#   * Order = method-id order (ids start at 2; 0/1 are __Result/__Callback).
#   * Once the catalogue is frozen this file is APPEND-ONLY: add a new action
#     at the END of its section and never reorder an existing line, because
#     doing so shifts later ids and breaks already-generated stubs. A retired
#     action cannot be parked as a reserved slot - actionc and action2tidl
#     reject a listed name with no matching .action file - so its line goes
#     and every id after it in that section shifts.
#
# Bootstrapped in alphabetical order from the tizen-action-catalog set
# (2026-10-01); ids from earlier bootstraps are not preserved. Until the
# catalogue is frozen the whole file is re-bootstrapped whenever the set
# changes, so no id here is stable yet. The [Tizen.Action.View] section is
# owned by the Common profile.

[Tizen.Action.AppAccount]
Tv_Tizen.Action.AppAccount_Get
Tv_Tizen.Action.AppAccount_GetProfiles
Tv_Tizen.Action.AppAccount_SwitchProfile
Tv_Tizen.Action.AppAccount_GetSubscriptionPlans

